# Build context for `docker compose build` / `docker compose up --build`.
#
# The Dockerfile creates every file it needs with heredoc COPY, so nothing in
# this folder has to reach the daemon. Keeping the context near-empty also
# keeps the 190 MB image tar out of it -- sending that on every build costs
# seconds and buys nothing.
#
# Add an exception here if you ever introduce a real `COPY <path>` from disk.

# Secrets and local configuration: must never enter an image layer.
.env
.env.example

# Build outputs.
*.tar

# Documentation and the Compose file: read on the host, never by the daemon.
*.md
docker-compose.yml

# Editor, VCS and OS noise.
.git
.gitignore
.cursor
**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
